    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0396" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/489</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Caperton to the
                            Secretary of the Navy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Everything quiet. Haitian Government stated that military officials under titles
                    of Commandants of Arrondissements, Chiefs of Sections, Commandants of Communes,
                    have been discharged throughout Haiti. Military and police functions will be
                    carried on by gendarmerie. One hundred nine detachments of constabulary
                    occupying one hundred nine different stations in Haiti. The country will be
                    thoroughly patrolled and order kept. Had conference with President and
                    Government Ministers today on various subjects. Attitude Haitian Government
                    always cordial. It expresses desire to carry out all wishes of United
                    States.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. B. Caperton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
